# Minecraft 26.2 — do not use these deprecated APIs

CE and older vanilla call sites often still use methods that are `@Deprecated` on 26.2. **Never port them as-is.** Look up the replacement in MCP `Minecraft-26.2` first.

## Chunk loaded checks

| Do not use | Use instead |
|---|---|
| `LevelReader.hasChunkAt(BlockPos)` / `hasChunkAt(x, z)` | On **`Level`**: `level.isLoaded(pos)` |
| `LevelReader.hasChunksAt(...)` | Loop `getChunkSource().hasChunk(chunkX, chunkZ)` (or keep a small local helper) |
| Blind `hasChunkAt` copy from CE | Same as above |

When the type is only **`LevelAccessor`** / worldgen (no `Level`):

```java
level.getChunkSource().hasChunk(
	SectionPos.blockToSectionCoord(pos.getX()),
	SectionPos.blockToSectionCoord(pos.getZ())
);
```

Apiculture already uses `Level.isLoaded` — match that when you have a `Level`.

## BoundingBox (immutable style)

| Do not use | Use instead |
|---|---|
| `box.encapsulate(BlockPos)` / `box.encapsulate(BoundingBox)` | `BoundingBox.encapsulating(a, b)` (returns a **new** box) |
| `box.move(dx, dy, dz)` / `box.move(Vec3i)` | `box.moved(dx, dy, dz)` |

Example:

```java
boundingBox = BoundingBox.encapsulating(boundingBox, new BoundingBox(pos));
```

## Habit

Before writing any method copied from Forestry CE / Immersive Forestry / old MC: check whether it is `@Deprecated` in `Minecraft-26.2`. If it is, use the replacement above (or search MCP for the new name). Prefer fixing the call site over `@SuppressWarnings("deprecation")`.
